WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.110 line:92%
- This is my first question, because I know that you're

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:04.120 line:92%
raised by a single mom that's a teacher as well.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.953 size:75% position:38% line:92%
- Me as well. - Yes.

00:00:04.953 --> 00:00:06.670 line:92%
My mom taught public school, fifth, sixth grade.

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.895 line:92%
She's retired now, the last couple of years,

00:00:08.895 --> 00:00:10.800 line:92%
so she want's two grandkids more.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.490 line:92%
But yes, she taught public school.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:14.540 size:75% position:38% line:92%
- Yeah mine did too!

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:15.920 line:92%
And when you went to film school,

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.930 line:92%
nobody ever did that for me, like Shannon did,

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:18.763 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
like her teacher.

00:00:18.763 --> 00:00:20.490 line:92%
Did you ever have anything like that kind of assignment?

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.430 size:78% position:39% line:92%
- No, no, not really.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.900 line:92%
I mean I knew because that was my mother's reason for

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:24.733 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
why I couldn't--

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:27.067 line:92%
you know, "can we get the Star Trek toy?"

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:28.033 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"No, we can't afford it"

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:28.866 size:88% position:44% line:92%
- [Kelly] "No, why not?"

00:00:28.866 --> 00:00:29.699 line:92%
- It was always, "we can't afford it."

00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:30.532 line:92%
- [Kelly] We were broke too!

00:00:30.532 --> 00:00:31.840 line:92%
- So I just thought we must be so poor!

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:32.881 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:00:32.881 --> 00:00:36.920 line:92%
- Because, but she definitely, well she did have one lesson

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.690 line:92%
that she kinda tried to impart to me growing up.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.566 line:92%
Well I really wanted a dog when I was a kid.

00:00:42.566 --> 00:00:43.680 size:78% position:39% line:92%
- Oh yeah, every kid!

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:44.930 line:92%
- A little house and a bath in here, and he'll bark.

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:46.900 line:92%
And you know, pretty normal, be in a park, whatever.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.210 line:92%
And my mom said, "you're not responsible enough

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:50.043 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to have a dog"

00:00:50.043 --> 00:00:50.876 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was 10.

00:00:50.876 --> 00:00:51.709 line:92%
I was like, "I am responsible enough!"

00:00:51.709 --> 00:00:54.370 line:92%
she said, "you're right, why don't you show me

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:58.500 line:92%
that you can do this? You have to walk the dog every day,

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.333 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
twice a day."

00:00:59.333 --> 00:01:00.190 line:92%
I said, "well okay, let's get the dog."

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:03.413 line:92%
She said, "no, first you have to walk an imaginary dog"

00:01:03.413 --> 00:01:04.680 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience laughs)

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:05.940 line:92%
I was like "it's, right, what do you mean?"

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.360 line:92%
she said, "twice a day, around the block as if you had

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.380 line:92%
the dog, so I know that you will do it

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:11.750 line:92%
and you're responsible enough to do it."

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.682 line:92%
So this woman, who I hope is watching,

00:01:14.682 --> 00:01:15.515 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience laughs)

00:01:15.515 --> 00:01:17.217 line:92%
gave me a leash! - I hope so too!

00:01:17.217 --> 00:01:21.019 line:92%
And I had to walk around the block with an empty leash.

00:01:21.019 --> 00:01:22.380 size:88% position:44% line:92%
- [Kelly] You look nuts!

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:23.213 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Twice a day.

00:01:23.213 --> 00:01:26.683 line:92%
And worse, we get to three weeks in and she's like--

00:01:26.683 --> 00:01:27.516 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- [Kelly] No!

00:01:27.516 --> 00:01:29.036 line:92%
- All right, forget it, I'm not giving you a dog!

00:01:29.036 --> 00:01:29.869 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(laughs)

00:01:29.869 --> 00:01:30.785 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience gasps)

00:01:30.785 --> 00:01:31.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- No!

00:01:31.618 --> 00:01:33.288 line:92%
- So she taught me the lesson of disappointment.

00:01:33.288 --> 00:01:34.956 line:92%
- [Kelly] Yeah, I was like, "you what?"

00:01:34.956 --> 00:01:35.789 size:78% position:39% line:92%
- Also came in handy.

00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:36.834 line:92%
- It's like all your hard work for nothing?

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:37.667 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- I know.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:38.575 line:92%
- That is not a good lesson.

00:01:38.575 --> 00:01:39.720 line:92%
- Well she was like, "I didn't think you were gonna

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:40.688 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
follow through!"

00:01:40.688 --> 00:01:42.896 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(laughing)

00:01:42.896 --> 00:01:44.210 line:92%
- Oh my god, so you never got the dog?

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.270 line:92%
- Yeah I didn't get a dog and then I thought

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:49.480 line:92%
I was so deprived I did like the dumbest thing you can do,

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.580 line:92%
which, that's the kind of thing you tend to do

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:52.413 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
when you're 18.

00:01:52.413 --> 00:01:53.280 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Which is how old I was.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.113 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:57.180 line:92%
- And as soon as I moved to LA and decided to be an actor,

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.120 line:92%
and had no money and no job.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:03.320 line:92%
And lived in a tiny apartment like, on Cherokee and Yucca

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:05.200 line:92%
over there in Hollywood, like.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.369 line:92%
I was like, "I'm getting a dog."

00:02:06.369 --> 00:02:07.500 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience laughs)

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.519 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- [Kelly] Damn it!

00:02:08.519 --> 00:02:09.617 line:92%
- So I went out and got a dog!

00:02:09.617 --> 00:02:12.077 line:92%
And not only get a dog but I got a husky.

00:02:12.077 --> 00:02:12.960 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience sighs)

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.413 line:92%
Which is like the most, you know, they don't have--

00:02:14.413 --> 00:02:15.246 size:78% position:39% line:92%
- That's a hyper dog.

00:02:15.246 --> 00:02:17.020 line:92%
- They only roam, they only wanna escape.

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:18.935 line:92%
You know what I mean, that's their like, mission in life.

00:02:18.935 --> 00:02:19.768 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah!

00:02:19.768 --> 00:02:21.410 line:92%
- But then I quickly realized like, "oh you have to get

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:25.014 line:92%
the dog food, and like the vet costs money!"

00:02:25.014 --> 00:02:26.116 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(laughing)

00:02:26.116 --> 00:02:26.949 line:92%
- You don't have to feed it!

00:02:26.949 --> 00:02:28.846 line:92%
- I was "I'm kinda going broke on this dog!"

00:02:28.846 --> 00:02:29.679 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience laughs)

00:02:29.679 --> 00:02:32.320 line:92%
Has a sad ending to this story though, which was that

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:36.130 line:92%
I used to leave the dog in a little space, shared space in

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.010 line:92%
the apartment when I went out, so he'd have some floor time,

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.341 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and the dog got stolen.

00:02:39.341 --> 00:02:40.174 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience sighs)

00:02:40.174 --> 00:02:41.460 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- That's wrong!

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.130 line:92%
- This was before the little microchips and stuff that you

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.510 line:92%
can put, you know, to track 'em down.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:46.343 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:46.343 --> 00:02:47.440 line:92%
- Yeah somebody stole the dog.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.410 line:92%
But it's telling that I didn't rush out and get another dog.

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.820 line:92%
- You're like, "you know what, the universe knew."

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:54.653 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Well, yeah.

00:02:54.653 --> 00:02:56.422 line:92%
Somebody has spoken and he was probably

00:02:56.422 --> 00:02:58.332 line:92%
not living his best life with me.

00:02:58.332 --> 00:02:59.410 line:92%
- [Kelly] I did the same thing.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:00.420 line:92%
- I'm sure he had a very happy life

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.813 line:92%
on a farm in Montana somewhere.

00:03:02.813 --> 00:03:05.270 line:92%
- I did the same thing though when I was young.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.740 line:92%
I was like, I think when you're out here, 'cause I moved

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:08.573 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
out here too.

00:03:08.573 --> 00:03:10.120 line:92%
And you want companionship or some kinda,

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.530 size:78% position:39% line:92%
you get a bit lonely.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.290 line:92%
So I did that too, it was a dumb move.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.610 line:92%
- Yeah I think when you have the least money,

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:16.890 size:75% position:38% line:92%
the smallest place--

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:17.820 line:92%
- [Kelly] You make the poorest decisions.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.050 line:92%
- And you're the dumbest.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.127 line:92%
You're like, "let me find another life

00:03:20.127 --> 00:03:21.929 size:84% position:42% line:92%
that can depend on me!"

00:03:21.929 --> 00:03:23.440 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(laughs)

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.120 line:92%
- 'Cause I'm holding it down solidly like myself.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.758 line:92%
- [Ben] Taken care of, yeah.

00:03:26.758 --> 00:03:28.660 line:92%
- All right come on guys let's go,

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:30.500 line:92%
we've got 15 seconds left.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.480 line:92%
We're gonna go on eight, gives us time for a rebound

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:33.460 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
or a tipple.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.290 line:92%
Brandon, 20's gonna pick you up full court, all right?

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:37.400 line:92%
Three, you're gonna come up and set

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.490 line:92%
the ball free for Brandon.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:39.880 line:92%
Brandon, you roll around to the right.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.042 line:92%
Garcia, come up as a back screen for Kenny.

00:03:42.042 --> 00:03:44.440 line:92%
Kenny, come out to the wing for the three.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.060 line:92%
Now then we got three options.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:48.420 line:92%
Brandon attack in right, or look for threes coming

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.440 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
off the screen.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.280 line:92%
But neither of those are there, go to Kenny for the

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.260 size:75% position:38% line:92%
three in the corner.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.412 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You got this okay?

00:03:53.412 --> 00:03:55.010 line:92%
Don't just nod, I wanna hear your voice.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:55.843 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yes or no?

00:03:55.843 --> 00:03:56.676 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yes coach.

00:03:56.676 --> 00:03:57.509 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(whistle blows)

00:03:57.509 --> 00:04:00.676 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(crowd cheers)

00:04:00.676 --> 00:04:02.138 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(clapping)

00:04:02.138 --> 00:04:02.971 line:92%
- Oh my god, it's such a great film.

00:04:02.971 --> 00:04:05.061 line:92%
Welcome back, I'm here with Ben Affleck!

00:04:05.061 --> 00:04:07.610 line:92%
And now here's a clip from his new film "The Way Back"

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:09.272 size:78% position:39% line:92%
which opens tomorrow.

00:04:09.272 --> 00:04:12.160 line:92%
So we'll talk about the film in a bit, but I did wanna

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:15.150 line:92%
ask you, is it true that you speak Spanish, like fluently?

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.350 size:84% position:42% line:92%
- I would say passably.

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:17.296 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- [Kelly] Passably.

00:04:17.296 --> 00:04:18.129 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yes I pass--

00:04:18.129 --> 00:04:19.310 line:92%
- I would love to even get to that point.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:21.426 line:92%
I feel like I can't, I always try but there's,

00:04:21.426 --> 00:04:24.360 line:92%
it's like unless you're like, immersed around it like,

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.160 line:92%
constantly I feel like it's just not gonna happen.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.640 line:92%
- That's the best way to learn for sure.

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:31.946 line:92%
I mean I did this like a little kids TV series

00:04:31.946 --> 00:04:35.750 line:92%
when I was young, and when I was 13, that season that year

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.290 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
was in Mexico.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:40.940 line:92%
So I was in Mexico for a year and that's how I picked it up.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:41.940 line:92%
So I learned how to like--

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:42.785 line:92%
- [Kelly] Oh when you were little.

00:04:42.785 --> 00:04:43.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:04:43.618 --> 00:04:44.451 line:92%
- It's easier when you're younger.

00:04:44.451 --> 00:04:45.284 line:92%
- And the brain when you're younger, yes.

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:48.860 line:92%
So you got the like, the older brain doesn't hold on

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:50.097 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to the information.

00:04:50.097 --> 00:04:53.700 line:92%
I wouldn't know myself, but that's what I, people have

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:54.980 line:92%
told me who are older. - 'cause we're so young!

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.260 line:92%
- We are both very young.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:57.213 line:92%
- That you remember but--

00:04:57.213 --> 00:04:58.046 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(laughs)

00:04:58.046 --> 00:04:59.360 line:92%
- So your kids speak Spanish?

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.970 line:92%
'Cause they teach all the languages now in schools,

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:01.803 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I've heard.

00:05:01.803 --> 00:05:03.640 line:92%
- My daughter's 14, and she's a very good student,

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:06.190 line:92%
and she's interested in Spanish, and so, I often help her.

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:08.800 line:92%
And now, she's all of a sudden got into the grade where

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:11.850 line:92%
she's like, in the harder Spanish classes and she's

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:12.683 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
getting better.

00:05:12.683 --> 00:05:15.840 line:92%
And she's like way at the point where I think she might

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:16.750 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
be passing me.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.092 line:92%
And that's when I was like, "no, this is not happening."

00:05:19.092 --> 00:05:19.925 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(laughing)

00:05:19.925 --> 00:05:21.570 line:92%
I don't mind that I can't do your math homework,

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:22.480 size:75% position:38% line:92%
you're 14 years old.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:23.328 line:92%
- But you will not be better.

00:05:23.328 --> 00:05:24.727 line:92%
But you're not gonna be better at Spanish than me.

00:05:24.727 --> 00:05:25.560 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience laughs)

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:27.750 line:92%
and so I've decided now I gotta like, take classes,

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:28.686 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I gotta do something--

00:05:28.686 --> 00:05:29.519 line:92%
- {Kelly] You gotta get a tutor.

00:05:29.519 --> 00:05:30.580 line:92%
- To keep up, because I can't have my 14 year old,

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:32.744 line:92%
she's like, "nah, that sounds ridiculous, you're not using

00:05:32.744 --> 00:05:34.450 size:75% position:38% line:92%
the imperfect tense"

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:36.674 line:92%
I'm just like, "I only know two tenses!

00:05:36.674 --> 00:05:39.830 line:92%
Now, before and future! That's all you need."

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:40.663 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah!

00:05:40.663 --> 00:05:42.420 line:92%
- Also the problem with Spanish is that you learn a bunch

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:43.830 line:92%
of words, like I don't know all these words.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:44.663 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:05:44.663 --> 00:05:46.360 line:92%
- In Mexico, some good, some, you know.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.193 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:47.193 --> 00:05:48.026 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Not for the show.

00:05:48.026 --> 00:05:48.859 line:92%
- Always a choice, I get it.

00:05:48.859 --> 00:05:49.692 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience laughing)

00:05:49.692 --> 00:05:51.470 line:92%
- And then you go somewhere else, like you go to Spain,

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:52.581 line:92%
or you go South America and they're like, "no, that's not

00:05:52.581 --> 00:05:53.820 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Spanish"

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.090 line:92%
I'm like, "what are you talking about, that's not Spanish?"

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:57.380 line:92%
And they go like, "I've never heard the word before

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.287 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in my life."

00:05:58.287 --> 00:05:59.120 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience laughs)

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.187 line:92%
And you're just like, "They say it in Mexico!"

00:06:00.187 --> 00:06:01.561 line:92%
"Mexico didn't speak real Spanish!"

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:02.394 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yes!

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:03.942 line:92%
- And then they're like, "you have a Mexican accent."

00:06:03.942 --> 00:06:04.775 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(laughs)

00:06:04.775 --> 00:06:06.629 line:92%
I was like, "hello, I don't have a Mexican accent"

00:06:06.629 --> 00:06:07.731 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I felt like--

00:06:07.731 --> 00:06:10.490 line:92%
I mean it's sort of like, the southern accent and,

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:11.323 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
you know, here.

00:06:11.323 --> 00:06:14.240 line:92%
Oh your, it's a little more like Australia, England

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:15.073 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and here.

00:06:15.073 --> 00:06:16.212 line:92%
We're like, you know, you go to Australia

00:06:16.212 --> 00:06:17.380 line:92%
and they'll be like, "oh mate (mumbles)"

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:18.213 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:18.213 --> 00:06:19.133 size:75% position:38% line:92%
- Like I don't know.

00:06:19.133 --> 00:06:19.966 line:92%
- Well you're good at all the things.

00:06:19.966 --> 00:06:20.799 size:84% position:42% line:92%
- What is a boobidiboo?

00:06:20.799 --> 00:06:21.632 line:92%
- You're good at all that.

00:06:21.632 --> 00:06:22.465 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Not really.

00:06:22.465 --> 00:06:23.298 line:92%
- Is it just 'cause you're exposed to it as an actor

00:06:23.298 --> 00:06:24.131 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at a young age?

00:06:24.131 --> 00:06:27.230 line:92%
- You know, I did a lot of, yeah I like to mimic.

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:29.060 line:92%
Like voices and stuff, when I was a kid.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.138 line:92%
I got a big kick out of that.

00:06:30.138 --> 00:06:31.647 line:92%
And so I used to like copy my friends voices and stuff.

00:06:31.647 --> 00:06:34.440 line:92%
And my father, when he lived with us, was a big

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:35.490 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Richard Pryor fan.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:36.323 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Oh yeah!

00:06:36.323 --> 00:06:38.330 line:92%
- Who was maybe one of, you know, the greatest stand-up

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.163 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
comedian ever.

00:06:39.163 --> 00:06:40.776 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But not PG!

00:06:40.776 --> 00:06:41.609 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(laughing)

00:06:41.609 --> 00:06:42.442 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience laughing)

00:06:42.442 --> 00:06:45.240 line:92%
I can remember, records would play, I was in second grade,

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:47.610 line:92%
third grade, fourth grade and I would imitate him and do

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:48.660 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
the jokes.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:50.143 line:92%
And he thought it was the funniest thing in the world.

00:06:50.143 --> 00:06:52.590 line:92%
And then one day we did like, bring dad to work day,

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:54.780 line:92%
and he came in to talk about being an auto-mechanic.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:55.860 line:92%
And I thought it was like, "oh now's a good time to launch

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:59.270 line:92%
into the Richard Pryor thing, that makes my dad laugh!"

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:00.664 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and he was like, "no!"

00:07:00.664 --> 00:07:01.810 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience laughs)

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:02.643 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Oh my gosh.

00:07:02.643 --> 00:07:03.680 line:92%
- I found out what it's like to be strangled by an

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:04.552 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
auto-mechanic.

00:07:04.552 --> 00:07:05.385 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(laughing)

00:07:05.385 --> 00:07:06.832 line:92%
- And that's when the parent's was like, "they've never

00:07:06.832 --> 00:07:09.317 line:92%
done this before, I don't know where it's coming from!"

00:07:09.317 --> 00:07:10.183 line:92%
- "Where did you hear this?"

00:07:10.183 --> 00:07:11.210 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(laughing)

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:12.620 line:92%
- I don't know what's happening!

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:14.670 line:92%
Okay well tell us about "The Way Back" tell us about

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:15.503 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
the new movie.

00:07:15.503 --> 00:07:17.780 line:92%
- We find this guy, very much like down on his luck.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:21.370 line:92%
He's drinking a case of beer a day, he's living in

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:24.220 line:92%
a kinda dingy apartment, he's, you know, he's got a job.

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:26.350 line:92%
He works construction, but he's separated from his wife,

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:28.640 line:92%
and you can tell he's not happy and he's not

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:29.490 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
engaged in life.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:30.323 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:07:30.323 --> 00:07:31.660 line:92%
- And throughout the course of the movie you start

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:34.200 line:92%
to find out kinda what happened that got him to that place.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:38.350 line:92%
And also he gets offered a job to coach the high school

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.382 line:92%
basketball team that he used to play for.

00:07:40.382 --> 00:07:41.850 line:92%
And he was like a big high school star.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.677 line:92%
He doesn't wanna do it, he's afraid, he's nervous,

00:07:43.677 --> 00:07:45.750 line:92%
but finally he takes the job.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:46.870 line:92%
You know, it's one of those things where he thinks

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:48.590 line:92%
he's gonna kinda come in and really coach them,

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:51.127 line:92%
and teach them and probably he gets more out of it,

00:07:51.127 --> 00:07:53.240 line:92%
the relationship, than the kids do.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.073 line:92%
- That's what I was gonna say, yeah.

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:56.560 line:92%
- It's really incredible and it doesn't pull any punches

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:59.650 line:92%
in terms of, life is hard, we're gonna have problems,

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:01.270 line:92%
you're gonna suffer, it's gonna be difficult.

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:03.270 line:92%
Sometimes really, really hard.

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:06.400 line:92%
But still says like, "things can get better."

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:07.233 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:07.233 --> 00:08:08.500 line:92%
- You can conquer your problem,

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.150 line:92%
you can climb over these walls.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:11.297 line:92%
You know, you can improve your life

00:08:11.297 --> 00:08:14.020 line:92%
and be hopeful and inspiring and that's what I really

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:14.853 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
loved about it.

00:08:14.853 --> 00:08:15.686 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:08:15.686 --> 00:08:16.960 line:92%
- And it's a joyful experience for me.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:19.210 line:92%
I really loved doing it, I loved those guys .

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:22.910 line:92%
It kinda rekindled my love for acting and, you know,

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:24.520 line:92%
I'm really proud of the movie.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.543 line:92%
- Yeah, it's one of those movies like, it means something,

00:08:26.543 --> 00:08:29.510 line:92%
it's like the message is so , it's not just like a movie

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:30.343 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
laugh-out-loud.

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:32.430 line:92%
And those are all great too, but I liked it had a

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:34.200 line:92%
really solid message, I like that like,

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.560 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and I always say this.

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:37.597 line:92%
We have a lot of different stories on this show.

00:08:37.597 --> 00:08:39.950 line:92%
Everybody's addicted to something, like,

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:42.750 line:92%
it might not be so obvious that it's alcohol for you,

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:43.800 size:78% position:39% line:92%
or drugs or whatever.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.230 line:92%
But everybody has that and I love the redemption

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:48.890 line:92%
factor in the film and I think it's very relatable.

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:50.640 line:92%
And is there a reason why you wanted to sign up

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:51.473 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to do this one?

00:08:51.473 --> 00:08:53.770 line:92%
- Yeah well, I mean for all those reasons.

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:55.570 line:92%
I agree with you like, compulsive behavior.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:57.610 line:92%
You know, we have this brain that works like

00:08:57.610 --> 00:08:58.750 size:81% position:41% line:92%
a reward center right?

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:02.070 line:92%
Like, our brain tells us like we eat food, and it sends

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:04.430 line:92%
a little bit of reward, dopamine or seratonin or whatever.

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:05.312 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Mine's sugar.

00:09:05.312 --> 00:09:06.145 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What?

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:06.978 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah.

00:09:06.978 --> 00:09:07.811 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience laughs)

00:09:07.811 --> 00:09:09.490 line:92%
- And so like you point out the fact like it's yes,

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:11.647 line:92%
you can look at things kind of isolated and also go,

00:09:11.647 --> 00:09:14.560 line:92%
"well that's an opioid addict problem, that's an alcohol

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:17.460 line:92%
problem, that's a compulsive shopping problem, that's

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:20.830 line:92%
anorexia, that's overeating, that's gambling, that's porn."

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:21.880 line:92%
and then all of a sudden--

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:22.713 line:92%
- It all comes from the same place.

00:09:22.713 --> 00:09:25.680 line:92%
- You see that basically it's a lot of different behaviors

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:28.470 line:92%
but what they're all trying to do is like, get out some

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:29.510 size:81% position:41% line:92%
feeling of discomfort.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:30.343 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:09:30.343 --> 00:09:32.150 line:92%
- You know, they're trying to solve that by doing something

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:34.310 line:92%
that is clearly not good for them, not healthy.

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:36.760 line:92%
You know it, mentally you know, in the front brain.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:39.160 line:92%
But that like, other part keeps asking for that reward

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:41.220 line:92%
and that good feeling and then you create kind of

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.420 line:92%
two minds like, "I know I don't wanna do this

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:44.470 line:92%
and yet I kinda can't stop."

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:46.150 line:92%
and that's when it goes from being you know,

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:48.630 line:92%
something healthy and celebratory, like alcohol should be.

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:50.396 line:92%
Great, have a drink, celebrate if you can do that.

00:09:50.396 --> 00:09:54.170 line:92%
To something that's like, you know, this is clearly

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.420 size:75% position:38% line:92%
not helping my life.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:56.253 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:09:56.253 --> 00:09:57.086 line:92%
- And yet I'm still doing it.

00:09:57.086 --> 00:09:58.655 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So why is that?

00:09:58.655 --> 00:10:01.400 line:92%
And I think the movie takes a good look at that

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.670 line:92%
in a way that's not, you know it's not a sermon,

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:04.503 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it's not a lecture.

00:10:04.503 --> 00:10:05.336 line:92%
That's like for church and school.

00:10:05.336 --> 00:10:06.407 size:84% position:42% line:92%
- It just humanizes it.

00:10:06.407 --> 00:10:07.750 line:92%
- You go to the movies to be inspired.

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:08.694 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:10:08.694 --> 00:10:10.440 line:92%
- And to find out that like, what was really important

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:13.066 line:92%
about me for that, you know, recovering alcoholic myself,

00:10:13.066 --> 00:10:17.130 line:92%
is that you're not defined by your problems.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:17.963 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:10:17.963 --> 00:10:18.796 line:92%
- That's not who you are.

00:10:18.796 --> 00:10:19.629 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:10:19.629 --> 00:10:20.462 line:92%
- Whatever it is, the issues,

00:10:20.462 --> 00:10:22.570 line:92%
you're not the bankrupt person, you're not the overeater,

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:24.869 line:92%
you're not the opioid, you're like, a whole big complicated

00:10:24.869 --> 00:10:26.690 line:92%
person and that's one part of it.

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:29.420 line:92%
And also, we tend to see those problems when they arrive

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:31.117 line:92%
in our lives and kind of sit in them and go,

00:10:31.117 --> 00:10:32.061 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"now I'm stuck."

00:10:32.061 --> 00:10:35.040 line:92%
You're not stuck, you can move past that stuff,

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:36.190 line:92%
you can change your life, you can make it better.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:37.279 size:88% position:44% line:92%
- [Kelly] Yeah, I agree.

00:10:37.279 --> 00:10:38.112 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(audience claps)

00:10:38.112 --> 00:10:39.974 line:92%
- I love though that the film though, humanized that.

00:10:39.974 --> 00:10:40.807 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
- Yeah.

00:10:40.807 --> 00:10:42.830 line:92%
- And it's just a really, really great message.

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:45.460 line:92%
Be sure to catch "The Way Back" in theaters tomorrow,

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:46.953 line:92%
I can't recommend it enough.

